[Music]  hello and welcome to playstation grenade  horizon forbidden west is one of the  most hotly anticipated games of the year  releasing on february 18th i thought now  is a great time to put together a video  about all the new things coming to  horizon forbidden west and how the game  has changed from horizon zero dawn so  whether you're an og horizon fan from  2017 maybe you first played when the  game was given away for free last year  or even if you thought eli was only a  character in fortnite here's everything  new in horizon forbidden west  the first thing you need to know is  about how to save yourself a little  money horizon forbidden west is only  available on ps4 and ps5 but get this  there is a free upgrade if you buy the  ps4 version the thing is the playstation  4 version is drastically cheaper than  the playstation 5 version so if you have  a ps5 and want to save 10 pounds or  euros simply buy the ps4 version and  freely upgrade to your current system  don't tell playstation i told you this  so let's set the scene the new story  picks up roughly six months after eloy  defeated hades in zero dawn i'll link a  story recap video if you need a  refresher the tribes we met now live in  harmony but suddenly a new issue arrives  a red blight covers the ground infecting  flora and fauna causing sickness and  superstorm spiral out of control in the  skies above the world needs saving again  so eloi picks up her spear again and  ventures into the new world the  forbidden west but where the heck is the  forbidden west well it's in the usa and  sees us traveling to the pacific ocean  via the mountains of utah passing  through the deserts of nevada  encountering new enemies and machines  along the way and we'll get to those  machines very soon in 2017 we started  with a combat spear for basic melee  action but quickly disregarded it in  favor of archery the developers have  seen this issue and made sure forbidden  west improves upon it as eloy spear is  now called to combat and just as  important as her bow improved striking  and a combo system will make eloy a  worthy opponent up close and personal  the idea is that we will freely change  up our attacks between spear and bow  during fights and to emphasize this we  have something called a resonator blast  by charging a power spear in melee  combat we can transfer that energy into  an enemy and then shoot them with an  arrow to cause massive damage another  addition sees this animation which i  cannot get enough of a loy has a limit  break this is the valor surge feature in  which eloy adds an effect to her weapon  before planting it in the ground and  affecting everyone around her to  activate valor surge players will have  to fill up an energy bar this is done by  accumulating combat xp from successfully  hitting headshots or removing components  from machines when the valasurge energy  bar is full enough players will be able  to unleash it there will be a total of  12 valor surges to unlock and they can  be upgraded along three tiers and  there's risk reward here the higher  level valor surges will take longer to  charge up but they will produce a far  more powerful attack to choose our valor  surges we must decide which skill tree  to upgrade in horizon zero dawn we have  three skill trees with a fourth added in  the dlc in forbidden west we have six  skill trees immediately all tied to play  style the skill trees are warrior hunter  trapper survivor infiltrator and machine  master our new skills are key to  fighting our new foes both machine and  man forbidden west's ai has been  considerably improved so much so that  enemy tribes have the ability to  override machines and fight with them in  unison for example a tremor tusk with a  raider on board will fight differently  to the machine if you found it in the  wilds which will then fight differently  from a group of human enemies without  any machine help a light will need to  react on the fly and change up her  playstyle to suit the adapting foes all  this has been done to force us to use  more of our weapons in our inventory  instead of finding that one overpowered  skill and spamming it continuously  combat variation looks to be more  improvised and intense  in 2017 horizon zero dawn released in  the same week as breath of the wild  which immediately changed our  expectations for open world gaming and  thankfully gorilla have taken note and  more elements from link's adventures  have found their way into forbidden west  free climbing is one of those updates we  desperately needed previously we were  ordered to use only a handful of ledges  to traverse whereas in forbidden west  much more of the world is ascendable  this isn't the total freedom of  something like gentian impact but it is  way more freedom this time around by  pushing r3 allies focus will scan the  area for ledges and outline them in this  yellow we also have access to the  pullcaster a kind of grappling hook  which lets aylei quickly reach high  areas or reposition almost immediately  useful to get the drop on enemies or  escape to fight another day it doesn't  stop there either now we can climb  higher and find new areas to discover we  need a way to safely get back down which  is why we have the shield wing nobody  wants to slowly climb back down a rock  face or mountain top we want to jump off  safely and that's why the shield wing is  perfect in addition to that climbable  world above us a new element of horizon  sees a world underneath beneath the  waves eloy once she obtains breathing  apparatus can now fully submerge and  freely swim around underwater visually  well look at it wow it's just stunning  but there are new mechanics under here  to be aware of underwater currents fight  back as we swim through them pushing a  light off course and of course there are  new machines in the waters too swimming  free climbing grappling hook and the  glider all these new elements  revolutionize alois traversal abilities  and we can even chain these skills  together to find secret new areas  let's go over to the settlements now hub  towns that eloy can freely visit in-game  the level of detail here is mind-blowing  and get this each npc has a timetable to  keep they have working times they have  sleep schedules and unique animations  the idea is to make settlements as  realistic as possible to hit home who  you are trying to save in this mission  and each of those settlements is  different it's unique to each tribe that  it represents this is a place to pick up  quests to upgrade gear with workbenches  to visit a stitcher to buy a new outfit  or take part in a melee pit a battle  area to fight against other tribesmen or  if you really want a challenge look out  for the arena a place to take on  machines in captivity in front of a  watching crowd gladiator style and each  of these challenges has a reward a piece  of loot a gear upgrade so maybe don't  leave these until after the credits roll  settlements are a great place to find  something new in horizon a new board  game played by the inhabitants of the  forbidden west machine strike it's  called we don't know much about it right  now but if gwent or orlog have taught me  anything these minigames will take up a  lot of our time one of the best things  about horizon zero dawn was a sidequest  system which saw people you helped  earlier in the game returning the favor  in the final battle this system has been  embraced fully in forbidden west in many  games you'll find that side quest givers  tend to vanish after that one single  transaction with them whereas in horizon  their impact is felt further they will  return later in the game and drop in and  out of the story never really fading  into the background better than that are  the improved rewards for completing side  quests in the forbidden west each extra  mission we choose could reward us with  something which drastically changes our  playstyle some of the side quests we  know about include hunting grounds you  know what that is salvage contracts in  which we must carefully dismantle a  machine in a fight for rare parts and  races are a thing too overriding  machines like hot wiring a car it looks  like there's a ton to do outside of the  car story  okay let's talk about the elephant in  the room new machines horizon forbidden  west is confirmed to have dozens of new  machine types living in the world there  will also be some returning from zero  dawn let's take a look at some of the  new ones the tremor tusk is a mammoth  beast with cannons on its side to ward  off flankers its charge and slam looks  devastating but its slow turning circle  appears to be the tremortusk's weakness  the clamber jaws are simian-like  creatures monkeying around these chaps  hunt in groups and climb to claim the  high ground above you just like obi-wan  the clawstriders are the velociraptors  of horizon yet their teeth are chainsaw  blades  rollerbacks are like a mechanical  armadillo with a tough protective shell  they will use these to roll into a ball  and squash you lovely shell snappers  remind me of the pokemon torterra a  tortoise-like being who hides in swamps  and marshlands around the forbidden west  a returning machine is the snapmaw but  now they have the water to freely swim  in we'll likely meet them under the  waves back in 2017 snap mars were  vulnerable to fire damage but i don't  think we can fight them that way when  we're underwater hmm the snapmore is  suddenly a much more potent predator and  then we have the pterodactyl-like sun  wings a flying machine cool fact their  wings are actually solar panels kool-aid  and my personal favorite is the  slitherfang a huge sand cobra which  moves and attacks like no other machine  continually moving slithering and  disappearing underground before  attacking without notice but that belly  does look quite weak so that's just  seven of the new machines that have been  revealed so far there are supposedly  dozens more to find for ourselves when  horizon forbidden west releases on  february 18th and to finish it all where  we started the ps4 and ps5 versions of  verizon forbidden west are indeed the  same game but of course there are  improvements on the playstation 5 you  should know about firstly everything  will look a little bit more impressive  draw distances detail lighting the real  changes though happen with load times as  the ps5 has that crazy fast ssd which  makes the game run with almost zero load  times elsewhere the audio on ps5 sees  improvement and of course the dual sense  controller offers haptic feedback and  adaptive triggers unlike the dual shock  the feeling of tension as your bowstring  pulls back never gets old it's really  cool but it isn't vital to play the game  the little touches which help immersion  are only available on playstation 5. so  there you go 20 new things coming to  horizon forbidden west i'm adam you're  awesome i'll see you next time

